faq:
  - q: "Is this website audit free?"
    a: "Yes. Enter any public website address and the examination runs on the engine at no cost, with no account. Public use is rate-limited per visitor to keep it available."
  - q: "What does the audit check?"
    a: "Seven areas: technical structure, SEO tags and files, document-level performance, accessibility markup, security headers, a sample of links, and content. Each finding shows its evidence and a fix."
  - q: "Is the score the same as Google PageSpeed or Lighthouse?"
    a: "No. Vector reads the HTML document and response headers; it does not run a browser, so it does not measure Core Web Vitals. It is a structural audit, and the methodology is printed with every report."
  - q: "Can I share the report?"
    a: "Every examination gets a permanent link. Send it to a colleague or a client, or save it as a PDF from the report."
  - q: "Will my website appear on the recently examined list?"
    a: "Only if you leave the listing option on when you run it. Untick it and the domain and score are kept private to the report link."
